# content/servers/dev — index routing topology for the `dev` environment.
#
# `rd index seed` (and `rd redeploy --run`) reads this and writes it into the env's
# index DB (resonantdust-dev-index-0) by calling the index module's reducers. The
# gateway then hands out these world servers; the world server resolves zone data
# to these shards. Clients never read this file or the index — only the gateway
# and the world server do.
#
# Format: whitespace-separated columns, one row per line; blank lines and lines
# starting with `#` are ignored. Row kinds:
#
#   server <server_id:u16> <ws_url>                  → set_server
#       A world server the gateway can allocate to a player. <ws_url> is what the
#       gateway returns to the browser, so it must be reachable FROM the client
#       (host-facing: ws://localhost:<server-port>/ws locally). 8xxx = server.
#
#   shard  <shard_id:u16>  <st_url> <db_name>        → set_shard
#       Where a data shard's SpacetimeDB DB lives. <st_url> is reached FROM the
#       world server (internal: http://start:3000 on the docker network).
#
#   region <region_id:u32> <shard_id:u16>            → assign_region
#       Route a region to a shard. Ids may be hex (0x…) or decimal. Only needed
#       for real multi-shard splits — with NO region row a region falls back to
#       the env's default shard (resonantdust-dev-region_shard-0), which is the
#       single-shard dev case. A region row REQUIRES its shard row to exist.

# One world server, the local dev game server on :8473.
server 0 ws://localhost:8473/ws

# One data shard — the dev region_shard DB on the shared local daemon. Not
# strictly required while everything falls back to the default shard, but states
# the topology explicitly and is ready for when regions get split out.
shard 0 http://start:3000 resonantdust-dev-region_shard-0

# Example region split (single-shard dev doesn't need this — the fallback covers
# every region). Uncomment + add more shards to route regions explicitly:
# region 0x00000000 0

#   cold <type_id:u8> <region:u8> <shard:u8> <st_url> <db_name>   → set_cold_shard
#       Route a (cold type, region) to a cold shard endpoint. type_id: 1 = biome-tile,
#       2 = biome-thing. <st_url> is reached FROM the world server (internal). The edge
#       resolves a zone's cold subscription through these rows; an unrouted region falls
#       back to the env's default (resonantdust-dev-{tile,thing}-0) while single-shard.
# Region 0 (around the origin — every visible zone today) → the local cold shards.
cold 1 0 0 http://start:3000 resonantdust-dev-tile-0
cold 2 0 0 http://start:3000 resonantdust-dev-thing-0
